2026-09-27T09:27:23.8284027Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8284340Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8284797Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8285265Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8285414Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8285766Z ================
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8285966Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8286219Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8286824Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8287577Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8287769Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8288301Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8288589Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8288807Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8289448Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8290066Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8291116Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8291931Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8292084Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8292700Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8293472Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8293884Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8294337Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8294927Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8295045Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8295304Z ========
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8295459Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8297551Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8299532Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8300005Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8300687Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8301754Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8302656Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8385244Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8386103Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8387071Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8387262Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8387669Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8387920Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8389675Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8391475Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8392462Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8393782Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:27:23.8394114Z 
